[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5388588624","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122714#issuecomment-5388588624","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122714","id":5388588624,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQS9WUA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-23T21:35:15Z","updated_at":"2026-08-23T21:35:15Z","body":"> This should slim down our build sizes\r\n\r\nIs this the main concern? If this is a performance PR, please measure the build size reduction by this change. Personally, I don't expect this to change the size beyond measurement variance, so I'd rather see this PR as a codestyle improvement than a performance improvement.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5388588624/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5389062300","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122714#issuecomment-5389062300","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122714","id":5389062300,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQTaQnA","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-23T23:24:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-23T23:24:32Z","body":"Well comparing the artifacts from our GHA between [this PR](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/32579968174) and [`master`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/32502831129/attempts/1), the size reduction seems to range from a few KB to over a MB. But that indeed could be measurement variance, so I'll take it with a grain of salt.\r\n\r\nMy other main goal with the PR was to unify codestyle for dummy references, so I am completely fine with saying this is a stylistic PR first and foremost. Will adjust the PR accordingly","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5389062300/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5913599803","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122714#issuecomment-5913599803","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122714","id":5913599803,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYHpfOw","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T14:43:45Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T14:43:45Z","body":"> I think if you make `CowData()`, `String()` and `StringName()` all `constexpr`, and then make `EMPTY` `constexpr`, there should be a few hundred kb saved too. Would be nice to get that in the same PR\r\n\r\nI don't think that can happen until C++20, where compilers got the logic to leverage `std::string` as `constexpr` within functions. Another one for the pile 🫠 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5913599803/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5913739730","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122714#issuecomment-5913739730","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122714","id":5913739730,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYHyB0g","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T14:51:34Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T14:51:34Z","body":"> > I think if you make `CowData()`, `String()` and `StringName()` all `constexpr`, and then make `EMPTY` `constexpr`, there should be a few hundred kb saved too. Would be nice to get that in the same PR\r\n> \r\n> I don't think that can happen until C++20, where compilers got the logic to leverage `std::string` as `constexpr` within functions. Another one for the pile 🫠\r\n\r\nIt can. I already tried it. Only the allocation constructors can't be `constexpr`; the empty ones that just assign `nullptr` can totally be `constexpr`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5913739730/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5914292541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122714#issuecomment-5914292541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122714","id":5914292541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYITxPQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T15:22:17Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T15:22:17Z","body":"> It can. I already tried it. Only the allocation constructors can't be `constexpr`; the empty ones that just assign `nullptr` can totally be `constexpr`.\r\n\r\nThe constructors aren't the problem; it's the *destructors* that cannot be `constexpr` until C++20.[^1] We can't even use builtin equivalents to `std::is_constant_evaluated` in C++17, as at least MSVC doesn't properly propogate the logic until C++20, and I believe a destructor is outright forbidden from using `constexpr` in C++17 even with extensions.\r\n\r\n[^1]:https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/constexpr","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5914292541/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5915211262","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122714#issuecomment-5915211262","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122714","id":5915211262,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYJL1_g","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T16:16:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T16:16:59Z","body":"Right, that makes sense.\r\n\r\nHowever, i don't think they need to be. The important part is that the string is initialized as `constexpr` to avoid it generating initialization checks on access.\r\n\r\nThe destruction can just happen on shutdown; it generates no additional code if it's not `constexpr`.\r\n\r\nFrom my tests, this pairing worked to reduce the size of e.g. `StringName::operator const String&`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5915211262/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5936751125","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122714#issuecomment-5936751125","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122714","id":5936751125,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYduiFQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T17:23:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T17:23:48Z","body":"No dice. While you can *technically* make the constructors `constexpr` on those types, that doesn't mean that the objects *themselves* can be made `constexpr`. Attempting to locally turn those three types' empty constructors `constexpr` does **not** allow turning `&EMPTY` into a `constexpr` variable. The reference is irrelevant here, as a standalone `EMPTY` will similarly fail.\r\n\r\nThis requires C++20. Full stop.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5936751125/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5939008732","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122714#issuecomment-5939008732","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122714","id":5939008732,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYf4U3A","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T19:30:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T19:30:44Z","body":"Drafted a C++20 equivalent of this PR with #124075, in case you wanted to test the idea firsthand","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5939008732/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused"